## Rows skipped
- A#3. Suggested drop of ", čl. 10" on the withholding-rate link. Tried it. The checker then failed 004 with `missing from translation (1): 10`, because the Korean source labels that link 영업세법 제10조. Restored ", čl. 10". The URL (flno=3) was not changed.
- A#4. Hangul in the 008/009 `url` values. ACCEPTED-ROUND: do not edit frontmatter `url`.
- A#26 space half, and B#34. Requests for a space thousands separator ("500 000", "1 579 589"). ACCEPTED-ROUND skip: cs is `NUMBER_THOUSAND_STYLE = dot`, and a space splits the numeral so the checker no longer sees one amount. Dot grouping kept. Part B amounts were already currency-after ("1.579.589 TWD"); only the separator was requested, so those figures were left unchanged.
- A#27. Removing the bare "1" in "poslední 1 rok", "na 1 přerušení", "za 1 den", "pro 1 poškozeného a 1 nehodu", "1 osobu", "dokončený 1 rok", "za 1 rok". Those digits are source quantities (one year, one day, one person, one victim, one accident, one suspension). Czech has no word-numeral lexicon in the checker, so "jeden" would not preserve the count. Digits kept.
- A#31 and B#17. Deleting U+200B, and turning 003 Q16–Q20 into `##` headings. ZWSP counts already match the Korean source exactly (003: 52, 005: 8, 006: 4, 008: 10, 009: 5, 013: 5, 015: 3). Heading levels must match the source too; Q16–Q20 are body lines there, as in the English file. A line that is only U+200B is a non-empty block. Deleting it, or adding headings, fails `blocks` or `headings`.

